{"episodes":{"161897":"Early morning thunderstorms produced several marine wind gusts.","161899":"An area of low pressure trekking over southwest Colorado was absorbed into a broader Pacific trough that lifted across the Western Slope. This led to scattered to widespread showers and thunderstorms. Some storms produced heavy rain which led to localized debris flows across portions of west-central Colorado over the course of a couple of days.","162564":"The combination of near normal moisture, light steering winds from Hurricane Sam passing well northeast of the area, and local and diurnal effects resulted in active afternoons across portions of interior and western on September 28th and 29th.","162631":"Write a Summary.","163122":"An upper level disturbance moving across south Texas produced scattered thunderstorms along the coast during the early morning hours on the 29th. Storms produced wind gusts to 35 knots except for one isolated stronger storm that produced wind gusts to around 45 knots near Corpus Christi Naval Air Station.","163162":"A dryline lead to numerous thunderstorm formation across portions of western and northern Texas and southwest Oklahoma. A few severe and hail and wind reports, along with reports of flooding, were received in and near Lawton, OK during the early evening on the 28th.","163163":"A dryline and weak upper wave helped initiate storms across far southwest Oklahoma and also in portions of northwest Oklahoma during the late afternoon. Storms persisted for several hours into the evening with a few reports of severe hail received.","163272":"An upper level low moved over Texas and interacted with a warm, moist airmass generating thunderstorms. Some of these storms produced damaging wind gusts, large hail, and heavy rain that led to flash flooding. Additional thunderstorms developed during the evening of the 30th.","163442":"An upper-level trough stretched from Utah southward into Arizona and a cold front near the Utah-Arizona border gradually moved southward triggering strong thunderstorms over far northern Arizona."},"events":[{"begin":"2021-09-29T00:04Z","county":"Comanche","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2021-09-29T00:04Z","endLat":34.61,"endLon":-98.41,"episode":163162,"id":985044,"injuries":0,"lat":34.61,"location":"1.14 W Lawton","lon":-98.41,"magnitude":1.0,"narrative":"Twitter photo.","source":"Social Media","state":"OK","type":"Hail","wfo":"OUN"},{"begin":"2021-09-29T00:12Z","county":"Bell","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"10.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2021-09-29T00:12Z","endLat":31.14,"endLon":-97.71,"episode":162631,"id":981906,"injuries":0,"lat":31.14,"location":"1.37 ENE Hood Afb","lon":-97.71,"magnitude":60.0,"magnitudeType":"MG","narrative":"A wind gust of 69 mph was measured at Fort Hood (KHLR). Military personnel reported an empty shipping container was pushed sideways in the strong wind. In addition, some minor structural damage occurred to a hangar door and some fencing. Some power poles were also down and tree limbs/branches were also knocked down.","source":"AWOS","state":"TX","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"FWD"},{"begin":"2021-09-29T00:20Z","county":"Bell","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"2.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2021-09-29T00:20Z","endLat":31.1357,"endLon":-97.5691,"episode":162631,"id":981909,"injuries":0,"lat":31.1357,"location":"4.1 W Tennessee Vly","lon":-97.5691,"magnitude":56.0,"magnitudeType":"EG","narrative":"Military personnel reported wind damage to trees and boat docks at their recreational facility on Lake Belton.","source":"Other Federal Agency","state":"TX","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"FWD"},{"begin":"2021-09-29T00:50Z","county":"Comanche","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"5.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2021-09-29T00:50Z","endLat":34.6,"endLon":-98.63,"episode":163162,"id":985045,"injuries":0,"lat":34.6,"location":"2.07 S Cache","lon":-98.63,"magnitude":61.0,"magnitudeType":"EG","narrative":"Gas station awning an